From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:05:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: apple-admac: do not access the registers at probe

On the T6040 (M4 Pro) the ADMACs of the AOP audio paths sit in a power
domain that the AOP firmware manages. They are powered only once the
AOP audio driver has requested an audio power state, which it does
right before its first channel request; a register access before that
faults.

Move the one-time CTL write of the split-bank controllers from probe to
the first channel allocation, done once under the carveout allocation
lock before the first SRAM carveout access.

Write the T603x UNK_28/UNK_2C values only after the slave config has
been validated, so that a refused config touches no register.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit f705806eac46578fed5373f38a67ef76c335ad7d)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/dma/apple-admac.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/apple-admac.c b/drivers/dma/apple-admac.c
index 0a63d4c504..d09b0697df 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/apple-admac.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/apple-admac.c
@@ -160,6 +160,7 @@ struct admac_data {
 	bool set_unk28;
 	bool evolved_layout;
 	bool split_channels;
+	bool ctl_programmed;
 	int irq;
 	int irq_index;
 	int nchannels;
@@ -645,6 +646,22 @@ static int admac_alloc_chan_resources(struct dma_chan *chan)
 	int ret;
 
 	dma_cookie_init(&adchan->chan);
+
+	/*
+	 * No register access at probe: on the T6040 the controller sits in a
+	 * power domain the AOP firmware manages, and it is only powered once
+	 * the audio driver has set the audio power state, before its first
+	 * channel request. The one-time CTL write is done here, before the
+	 * first carveout access.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&ad->cache_alloc_lock);
+	if (!ad->ctl_programmed) {
+		if (ad->split_channels)
+			writel_relaxed(0x18080001, ad->base + REG_CTL);
+		ad->ctl_programmed = true;
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&ad->cache_alloc_lock);
+
 	ret = admac_alloc_sram_carveout(ad, admac_chan_direction(adchan->no),
 					&adchan->carveout);
 	if (ret < 0)
@@ -834,11 +851,6 @@ static int admac_device_config(struct dma_chan *chan,
 	u32 bus_width = readl_relaxed(ad->base + REG_BUS_WIDTH(ad, adchan->no)) &
 		~(BUS_WIDTH_WORD_SIZE | BUS_WIDTH_FRAME_SIZE);
 
-	if (ad->set_unk28) {
-		writel_relaxed(T603X_UNK_28_VAL, ad->base + REG_UNK_28);
-		writel_relaxed(T603X_UNK_28_VAL, ad->base + REG_UNK_2C);
-	}
-
 	switch (is_tx ? config->dst_addr_width : config->src_addr_width) {
 	case DMA_SLAVE_BUSWIDTH_1_BYTE:
 		wordsize = 1;
@@ -876,6 +888,11 @@ static int admac_device_config(struct dma_chan *chan,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	if (ad->set_unk28) {
+		writel_relaxed(T603X_UNK_28_VAL, ad->base + REG_UNK_28);
+		writel_relaxed(T603X_UNK_28_VAL, ad->base + REG_UNK_2C);
+	}
+
 	writel_relaxed(bus_width, ad->base + REG_BUS_WIDTH(ad, adchan->no));
 
 	/*
@@ -1002,9 +1019,6 @@ static int admac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, err,
 				     "unable to trigger reset\n");
 
-	if (ad->split_channels)
-		writel_relaxed(0x18080001, ad->base + REG_CTL);
-
 	err = request_irq(irq, admac_interrupt, 0, dev_name(&pdev->dev), ad);
 	if (err) {
 		dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, err,
